      <div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">00:01</div><div class="transcript-line">Hello, this is April 1st, 2009. My name is Carrie Gutierrez. I&#39;m the Assistant Curator of Collections at the First Division Museum at Cantigny.</div><div class="timestamp">00:10</div><div class="transcript-line">I am interviewing Shannon Morgan at the McCormick Research Center at the First Division Museum at Cantigny, located in Wheaton, Illinois. Okay. The first question I want to ask you, Shannon, is when did you enter the Army?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">00:26</div><div class="transcript-line">Uh November of 2001.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">00:28</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">00:29</div><div class="transcript-line">And why? Uh for the college money, my family&#39;s not very rich, so um basically I wanted uh a chance to further my education.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">00:38</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">00:39</div><div class="transcript-line">And plus 9-11, I didn&#39;t want that happening again.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">00:43</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay. So it was very much in response to the Exactly.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">00:46</div><div class="transcript-line">I joined pretty much immediately afterwards.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">00:48</div><div class="transcript-line">Wow.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">00:49</div><div class="transcript-line">So</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">00:51</div><div class="transcript-line">So tell me about joining the 1st Infantry Division.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">00:55</div><div class="transcript-line">It was exciting. First of all, I went to BASIC and Fort Jackson, South Carolina. Then I went on to my MOS School for Track Vehicle Mechanic in Aberdeen Proving Grounds, Maryland. And then to my first duty station at Fort Riley, Kansas.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">01:10</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay. How were you received into your unit?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">01:15</div><div class="transcript-line">Um well I was the only tracked vehicle mechanic at Fort Riley, female anyways, so I was in a 37-man all pl all-man platoon, all males Uh it was definitely different. Uh at first they didn&#39;t know what to do because they didn&#39;t want some sissy female working with them. But it took about five minutes for them to realize that I was gonna be able to hang.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">01:36</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay. Okay. So you they They accepted you quickly?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">01:41</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay. Definitely.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">01:42</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay. What when you you know at first you said it was a little it was a little tough.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">01:47</div><div class="transcript-line">Yeah, I was walking in with my platoon sergeant who come and picked me up at receiving uh and I heard the guys talking in the motor pole and they&#39;re like, Oh no, here comes a girl, we&#39;re not gonna be able to cuss and do our dick and fart jokes or whatever and so uh it took about five minutes for me to opening my mouth and having a conversation. They were like, oh she&#39;s cool. So nothing to worry about.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">02:07</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay. Well that&#39;s good. It&#39;s good What kind of training did you receive?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">02:12</div><div class="transcript-line">Um, I received the MOS school for tracked vehicle mechanic, which was about 12 weeks.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">02:17</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay. What is what does um that include?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">02:21</div><div class="transcript-line">I work on all the tanks. Anything that has track on it, um I worked on that.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">02:25</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay, so any repairs, any repairs, maintenance.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">02:28</div><div class="transcript-line">Maintenance, driving them, fixing them, mm-hmm, all of that.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">02:31</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay. Did you did you have any experience with that before or they kind of taught you everything?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">02:36</div><div class="transcript-line">Yeah. Um not with tanks or anything like that, but I had uh mechanical knowledge because my father uh growing up I was tomboy of course and he would show me how to fix something once and if I didn&#39;t pay attention then the next time I had to pay for it to fix it.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">02:51</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">02:52</div><div class="transcript-line">So I had a little bit of a mechanical incline knowledge to that.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">02:55</div><div class="transcript-line">Yeah Okay. So what were your those were I think you kind of pretty much covered then your duties before getting into Team Lioness. Okay. So what were your duties specifically in Team Lioness?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">03:10</div><div class="transcript-line">Uh we were we were as assigned to um assist the males in searching the Iraqi women because uh it started to portray out where um the males would give the women all of their explosives and their detonators and uh pertinent information they would give it to the women because in Iraq uh American soldier males are not allowed to touch the women.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">03:34</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">03:34</div><div class="transcript-line">According to their religion.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">03:36</div><div class="transcript-line">Mm-hmm.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">03:37</div><div class="transcript-line">So that&#39;s where they saw the need for us to come in and bring females to search them.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">03:42</div><div class="transcript-line">I see. So they would give it to the women in thinking that no one would search them so it was safe with them. Exactly.</div><div class="timestamp">03:49</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay. Now in the film I um I believe there was there was some parts. How much was I think there was you you talked about comforting the women.</div><div class="timestamp">03:57</div><div class="transcript-line">Was that a major part of it or was it really just, you know, doing the search?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">04:02</div><div class="transcript-line">Um, it was a little bit of both because once they realized that we were uh women ourselves They started giving up information about telling us where major players were hiding out, uh people we were looking for.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">04:14</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">04:15</div><div class="transcript-line">And they ended up giving us a lot of intel that the male soldiers would not have been able to re to get</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">04:21</div><div class="transcript-line">Now did they realize that when they&#39;re telling you these things, I mean this is information that you&#39;re after? With I mean did they how readily did they give up the information?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">04:30</div><div class="transcript-line">Well, it would have to be when they were away from their husbands and families. So we would pull them into different rooms away from, you know, separate them away from their men and as soon as we did that they&#39;d start talking to us. Uh the women were actually they wanted the war to end and they wanted all the the violence to stop.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">04:47</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">04:48</div><div class="transcript-line">So That&#39;s why they would speak with us.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">04:50</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay, so they they trusted the lionuses fairly quickly.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">04:55</div><div class="transcript-line">Exactly.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">04:56</div><div class="transcript-line">What do you think um What do you think how do you think that they perceived you, you know, in their culture seeing women co you know, soldiers in combat. How do you think they react to that?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">05:07</div><div class="transcript-line">I think I think they were in a little bit of admiration almost because the women over there are treated very badly. I mean they&#39;re not even allowed to walk side by side next to their husband. When they ride in a car they have to sit in the back seat.</div><div class="timestamp">05:19</div><div class="transcript-line">Mm-hmm. Uh they always have to be three steps behind him. And uh there&#39;s usually five of &#39;em, uh five wives per man, depending on their income.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">05:29</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">05:29</div><div class="transcript-line">So</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">05:30</div><div class="transcript-line">Wow.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">05:30</div><div class="transcript-line">I think they w I think they kinda looked up to us almost having in that freedom, so to speak.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">05:36</div><div class="transcript-line">Yeah. Did did you ever have a conversation with one of them where any of them addressed any of the Wolves women addressed that or anything?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">05:42</div><div class="transcript-line">Um not necessarily. I mean the only the only places um they spoke real um they spoke English really well was like at the schools and things like that and those were teachers who were teaching. Um the schools are separated as well, all females and all males.</div><div class="timestamp">05:58</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay. So, um, most of the time those kind of women didn&#39;t really want to talk to us too much. They just wanted us out of their school so they could get back to teaching.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">06:06</div><div class="transcript-line">Yeah, okay. So when you were taught how to search these women, did you I mean was there anything that was really kind of outstanding or was it a basic search or basically just a basic search like airport security. Okay It&#39;s a good way to Yeah. Okay. Um did you so did you feel like your training for, you know, in in theory what you were supposed to do is, you know, your job as a lioness, did you feel it was adequate for what you ran across?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">06:37</div><div class="transcript-line">Not when we started to encom uh to encounter combat, no, because we&#39;re not trained to be infantry soldiers. It&#39;s against DOD policy for women to be in frontline ground combat. So we had no experience in that sort of training whatsoever.</div><div class="timestamp">06:50</div><div class="transcript-line">I mean we had basic training, but they don&#39;t train you like they do the men that are infantry. So um absolutely not. I don&#39;t believe we had enough training whatsoever.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">06:59</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay Okay. So your your mission, as you understood it as as a lioness, was basically to go in with with the Marines or, you know, and and do these searches. Correct.</div><div class="timestamp">07:13</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay. Okay. What was your first operation as a lioness?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">07:18</div><div class="transcript-line">Oh goodness. My f my yeah. My first one, myself and uh good friend of mine, specialist Stone, was attached to one five Um, which is Army of course.</div><div class="timestamp">07:28</div><div class="transcript-line">Um anyways, uh we had to go out and do a Was it a knock and greet or was the first one a bug hunt? Gosh, so many of &#39;em. I believe the first one was just a knock and greet.</div><div class="timestamp">07:42</div><div class="transcript-line">We were trying to get out there and get the word out, um, that we&#39;re friendly, we&#39;re here to win hearts and minds and And basically that&#39;s what it consisted of.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">07:51</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay, okay. The other one that you mentioned, the what hunt. What does that mean?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">07:56</div><div class="transcript-line">Bug hunt was what code words we use when we were looking for specific uh high value targets.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">08:01</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay, okay. Now is that Ramadi? Okay that we talked that you talked about in the DVD?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">08:08</div><div class="transcript-line">Like the uh the deck of cards. That you guys have probably heard of, um, with high value targets on it.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">08:15</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">08:15</div><div class="transcript-line">That&#39;s what we did. We went out and arrested these people.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">08:18</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay. So your first mission it did it go well?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">08:21</div><div class="transcript-line">Absolutely, yeah. It was it was pretty fun. I was scared to death, of course. um in the back of stack teams and uh but it it went really well. I mean it was just basically going in and checking things out and making sure they had no weapons of mass destruction of course and and uh we didn&#39;t find anything so</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">08:40</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">08:40</div><div class="transcript-line">We returned back to base.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">08:41</div><div class="transcript-line">So after that you felt a little more comfortable?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">08:44</div><div class="transcript-line">Yes. Okay. Yeah, well kind of. And so we got hooked up with the Marines because one five field artillery is still army, so</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">08:54</div><div class="transcript-line">What would you you know there was a lot in the DVD about, you know, um government policy, et cetera, and you know how what happens in practice in Team Lioness, how it conflicts with that. What would you want to say to government officials ab about being a lioness, the existence of lionesses and the role of women&#39;s service in the military as a whole?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">09:18</div><div class="transcript-line">Um, I would say that in the beginning, um even Mr. Donald Rumsfeld himself was denying that we were even doing it. Um So that was kind of a a sharp stick in the eye. But uh anyways, I think women are capable. Uh faces of war have changed and we&#39;re moving ahead and uh I would definitely say to them that if they want us to play infantry, that they should allow us to be infantry. Okay.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">09:47</div><div class="transcript-line">So there&#39;s a lack of knowledge and publicity about what lionesses do. If you were if you were to write the message to the public now, what would you have it say?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">09:58</div><div class="transcript-line">Oh goodness. Um that team line us is Well, just from my own experience, Team Lion S was the first female uh combatant unit, so to speak, if you will. Um, I would I would let the public know that uh women are out there doing the same thing that the m uh male infantry soldiers are doing now.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">10:26</div><div class="transcript-line">Mm-hmm.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">10:27</div><div class="transcript-line">And uh I don&#39;t know, I guess that&#39;s it.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">10:31</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay. You would just want to inform them that it is indeed taking place.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">10:35</div><div class="transcript-line">Exactly. It still continues on to this day.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">10:38</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay. How prevalent are lionesses? Is it is it just in the first division or Um no actually it&#39;s it&#39;s army wide from what I understand.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">10:48</div><div class="transcript-line">Um more and more units are using it and actually the Marines are using uh lineasses now out of their own segregations. Okay.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">10:58</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay. So it&#39;s fairly widespread. Do you have any idea how many trained or helped?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">11:03</div><div class="transcript-line">Yeah, I have no idea.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">11:05</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay. Okay. So you th well, do you think that women should be allowed in direct combat? Why or why not?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">11:12</div><div class="transcript-line">Absolutely. Um there are women that are very capable of doing it. Um I believe that uh You know, we&#39;re in a new era.</div><div class="timestamp">11:21</div><div class="transcript-line">We&#39;re fighting different kinds of wars. And uh I believe women are just as capable as men these days. And I think uh I think we deserve to be there right side by side.</div><div class="timestamp">11:32</div><div class="transcript-line">They push for all kinds of equality in the Army and we bunk together, we sleep together, we fight together, we train together. So I absolutely believe we deserve to be in direct ground combat.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">11:43</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay. I mean have those uh expired for that you feel do you feel those have expired for why women were not you know are not allowed allowed to be able to do that.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">11:56</div><div class="transcript-line">Yes, absolutely, yeah. I I think uh I think the chauvinistic side of it has uh started to um go down. I I mean, I don&#39;t think that people are quite as quite as chauvinistic as they used to be because, you know, uh this is the twentieth century and and we&#39;re moving ahead. Women do a lot more these days than they did back then.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">12:24</div><div class="transcript-line">Right. Um, who who has helped you the most in dealing with your military experiences and your memories?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">12:35</div><div class="transcript-line">Um, the VA counselors. Uh there was one in particular, her name was Michelle Leva and she was the first person I spoke to when I went to the VA. Um, she was really there for me, her and my uncle.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">12:48</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay. Okay.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">12:49</div><div class="transcript-line">Because your uncle was the He was a three tour of Vietnam, but yeah, he was the only man left returning from his company.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">12:55</div><div class="transcript-line">Wow. Okay. But it helps to have family, you know. Yeah. Somebody who&#39;s who&#39;s always there with you supporting you.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">13:02</div><div class="transcript-line">Exactly.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">13:04</div><div class="transcript-line">Um At at at the VA what did do you mind me asking? What are some of the things that like how did she help you or</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">13:13</div><div class="transcript-line">Um, basically she just let me rant and rave, uh, when probably most psychologists wouldn&#39;t let you get that uh crazy. But uh she was always there for me. Um I think she knew when I was scared to talk about things and I think she also knew how to approach it Um she had only dealt with male um uh soldiers for the most part, but it it was it was just so weird because there was a certain comfort level there between us and uh She she just she had my back the whole time.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">13:49</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay. Did she happen to notice any or communicate to you any difference between you know, you dealing you as a woman dealing with your experiences as opposed to men, she&#39;s a little bit of a you know, men are more pent up and they don&#39;t open up as much as</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">14:06</div><div class="transcript-line">women do and they tend to to wait until it&#39;s too late.</div><div class="speaker">Speaker 3</div><div class="timestamp">14:10</div><div class="transcript-line">Mhm.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">14:10</div><div class="transcript-line">I mean there are, you know, a lot of a lot more soldiers that are males that attempt suicide than females. Okay. So, I mean it&#39;s like She just knew.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">14:22</div><div class="transcript-line">Mm-hmm. So do you still talk to her or um no not at this point.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">14:28</div><div class="transcript-line">She switched VAs. Um she&#39;s went to a different location and I&#39;m not in contact with her anymore.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">14:35</div><div class="transcript-line">How long did you spend with her?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">14:37</div><div class="transcript-line">About a year and a half.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">14:38</div><div class="transcript-line">Wow, okay. And you felt that it did you feel it helped and Um how have your military experiences changed the way you view the world?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">14:52</div><div class="transcript-line">It&#39;s made me a a stronger person. I don&#39;t take anything for granted anymore, not even toilet paper.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">14:57</div><div class="transcript-line">Wow.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">14:58</div><div class="transcript-line">But yeah, um it&#39;s definitely giving me a new perspective and and it really uh like when fourth of july rolls around you really understand what it&#39;s all about.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">15:07</div><div class="transcript-line">Mm-hmm.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">15:08</div><div class="transcript-line">That freedom doesn&#39;t come free.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">15:10</div><div class="transcript-line">Right. Um, and you say that what what what from your military experiences, um, maybe in particular, is there anything in particular that that causes you to, you know, feel this way?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">15:24</div><div class="transcript-line">I think watching your best friend die. Uh yeah. I think that would have a lot to do with it and the camaraderie that you build being together in a war zone we&#39;re actually closer than family members are. And um being over there fighting for this country gives you a real sense of pride.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">15:42</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay. Absolutely, I can imagine. What advice or thoughts would you share with future women soldiers in combat situations?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">15:54</div><div class="transcript-line">I I would say to them, don&#39;t hold back. Uh you can never hesitate. And don&#39;t forget that just because you&#39;re a female, it doesn&#39;t make you incapable of anything.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">16:04</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay. It&#39;s good advice. Yeah. Hmm. Given the work that Team Linus has done, do you think the government will uh change the rules for women in combat and you know if so when do you when do you think this might happen?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">16:20</div><div class="transcript-line">I think I think we&#39;re moving to a new stage de with that, definitely. Um we just left Washington D C and uh we spoke to several people who are in charge of making those policies.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">16:32</div><div class="transcript-line">Mm-hmm.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">16:33</div><div class="transcript-line">So um I believe there&#39;s a very good chance that uh Something could change.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">16:38</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">16:39</div><div class="transcript-line">Definitely. I d I have no idea when it&#39;s the government. They do what they want, so but uh They they they really seem to be very interested in it. And um I think they see now that women are capable of this.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">16:53</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay. Um tell me more about, you know, your trip to Washington, what happened, who did you talk to, what was discussed?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">17:00</div><div class="transcript-line">Um well we met with uh Senator Barbara Davis from California, which she sits on the Congress. Yes, that&#39;s it. Yes. She says it&#39;s on what?</div><div class="speaker">Speaker 3</div><div class="timestamp">17:21</div><div class="transcript-line">She is the um chairman of the subcommittee on the assignment of uh on military personnel okay right uh my gosh there&#39;s so many people we met I can&#39;t remember them all but uh</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">17:36</div><div class="transcript-line">Yeah um I got to meet uh Blanche Lincoln from Arkansas.</div><div class="speaker">Speaker 3</div><div class="timestamp">17:41</div><div class="transcript-line">Um Senator Blanche Lincoln Senator um The one from Washington, Senator Patty Murray. Okay.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">17:49</div><div class="transcript-line">And Nancy Pelosi gave us the the speaker of the House, right? That were flown um at the Capitol in honor of us.</div><div class="speaker">Speaker 3</div><div class="timestamp">17:58</div><div class="transcript-line">Wow. Chairman Filner.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">18:02</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay.</div><div class="speaker">Speaker 3</div><div class="timestamp">18:03</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">18:04</div><div class="transcript-line">No, it&#39;s fine. I&#39;m just thinking, I don&#39;t think you have a microphone on you. Okay, okay. Yeah.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">18:10</div><div class="transcript-line">I&#39;m sorry, I just can&#39;t remember all these people.</div><div class="speaker">Speaker 3</div><div class="timestamp">18:12</div><div class="transcript-line">And Congresswoman Stephanie Hurseth Sandlin from South Dakota and Congresswoman Judy Biggert from Henry. Yep. Um they were all on the panel. Okay. And then we did a press side a press event on the Senate side and there were two women senators who came and Shannon spoke.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">18:30</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay. Okay Yeah, I was just gonna say um you&#39;re you are the director. Well I&#39;ll let you introduce yourself.</div><div class="speaker">Speaker 3</div><div class="timestamp">18:40</div><div class="transcript-line">I&#39;m Meg McClagan, the co-director of Director documentary Lion S. Okay.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">18:46</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay. Thank you. Thank you. So when you went to Washington did all of these people um they all saw the DVD while you while you were there?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">18:55</div><div class="transcript-line">If not had they seen a clip. that they put together a 20-minute clip.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">18:59</div><div class="transcript-line">I see.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">18:59</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay. So they got to see that if they hadn&#39;t seen the DVD, but I&#39;m sure some of them have.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">19:05</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay. So how did those how did those conversations go? What was discussed? What did they ask you?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">19:10</div><div class="transcript-line">Um they asked us a lot on policy change and what they could do to make it better for women for females in the military. Um Also, uh VA services, uh, because I use the VA a lot now, um, asked us how they could improve that and what they need to do, what steps they should take, things like that nature.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">19:31</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay Okay. Did you was there anything that you wanted to kind of share about some of the feedback you know you gave to them um in in those meetings, in those conversations, discussions?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">19:42</div><div class="transcript-line">One of my big um quirks was I told them we needed more women therapists because there was a lack of women therapist in the in the VA hospitals Um, the first time I ever went um to a psychologist, if you will. Um, this is after I had received my 100% for being PTSD Um, he basically didn&#39;t believe me that I&#39;d ever been in frontline combat. He couldn&#39;t fathom the concept of women being in combat.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">20:08</div><div class="transcript-line">Wow.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">20:09</div><div class="transcript-line">So I there&#39;s a there&#39;s a great need for women therapist in the VA and that&#39;s what I told him.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">20:14</div><div class="transcript-line">Mm-hmm I&#39;m sorry, you d a few a few seconds ago you just said oh you were when you were This is this is my psychologist that I was assigned to.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">20:22</div><div class="transcript-line">We have teams and things like that.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">20:24</div><div class="transcript-line">Right. Like they&#39;ve got to be able to do that.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">20:28</div><div class="transcript-line">100% disabled.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">20:29</div><div class="transcript-line">I see. Okay. That&#39;s okay. Just want to clarify what that meant.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">20:32</div><div class="transcript-line">Yes, 100% disabled.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">20:34</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay. What what happened in Washington? Did they um did they record that That whole thing was a little bit more than a little bit of a little bit of a little bit of a little bit of a little bit of a little bit of a little bit of a little bit of a little bit of a little bit of a little bit of a little bit of a little bit</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">20:40</div><div class="transcript-line">They had they had their people with them that wrote down everything, yes.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">20:43</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay, okay.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">20:44</div><div class="transcript-line">Their assistants or whatnot.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">20:46</div><div class="transcript-line">I see. Okay. Yeah Um you know, you you you and your uncle talked in the D V D about questioning what you&#39;ve done and in particular I noticed I keyed on in on the fact that you you use you use the word justice. Um and you also said in the DVD that you can&#39;t help dwelling on the memories and and wondering In going over the memories time again, time and again, have you found any any justice and what would make what would make it justified?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">21:21</div><div class="transcript-line">Hmm. I don&#39;t think there is justice or more. Um basically I just had to accept the fact we did what we did and we did it for a reason and let go and and live on for the people who didn&#39;t make it home.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">21:34</div><div class="transcript-line">Mm-hmm.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">21:35</div><div class="transcript-line">I guess that&#39;s all I can really say about that one.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">21:37</div><div class="transcript-line">That&#39;s a little Yeah.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">21:38</div><div class="transcript-line">Yeah.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">21:39</div><div class="transcript-line">Yeah.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">21:39</div><div class="transcript-line">I might start balling on you.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">21:41</div><div class="transcript-line">Well, I&#39;m ready. Yeah, now I understand. Okay. Um you know, you you talked in the DVD again about um the Marine Squad that you were with in Ramadi that you you mentioned tapping back that the person from what I uh what I gathered from that is the person In front of you is supposed to tell you, hey, we&#39;re moving.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">22:04</div><div class="transcript-line">Right.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">22:04</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay. And they left you.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">22:07</div><div class="transcript-line">Correct.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">22:07</div><div class="transcript-line">Whatever I mean, so you said that they didn&#39;t tap back But did you ever find out? I know you got back to that unit. What happened?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">22:15</div><div class="transcript-line">As of yesterday I was informed by a female Marine that they use hand signals which there was no hand signals to be used but anywho I&#39;m not gonna argue with her um Being a sawgunner, I was a two four a two four nine sawgunner, so that means I carried a big machine gun.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">22:31</div><div class="transcript-line">Right.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">22:32</div><div class="transcript-line">So I covered everybody&#39;s asses and butts, I&#39;m sorry, in front of me. Um, so it&#39;s important to let the person covering your rear know that you&#39;re moving.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">22:41</div><div class="transcript-line">Right.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">22:41</div><div class="transcript-line">And uh from what I understand from her uh that they have three four man teams that move on their own and they&#39;re not used to integrating females which we weren&#39;t used to being with males. So I mean there was just a lot of miscommunication, but I think they might have fixed some of that by now.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">23:00</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">23:01</div><div class="transcript-line">I hope so anyway.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">23:02</div><div class="transcript-line">Is that was that kind of the, you know, lack of some of the mistraining maybe too?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">23:07</div><div class="transcript-line">Not so much that, it&#39;s the difference between the different branches.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">23:10</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">23:10</div><div class="transcript-line">We all do different things. We all move differently, we all fight differently.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">23:14</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay. Yeah, you talked about that in the DVD how there was It just they Marines can operate differently. Exactly.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">23:20</div><div class="transcript-line">So that just they assumed probably They assumed that we had already had that training, the same training our our men received.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">23:26</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">23:27</div><div class="transcript-line">Which we didn&#39;t.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">23:28</div><div class="transcript-line">Got it Okay. Um as so you said as soon as you set foot in Iraq, you said that you felt like you lost a part of you. I&#39;m sure it&#39;s very difficult to put that into words, but you know, when you said that in the DVD, if you can, I was hoping you could just talk a little bit more about that.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">23:49</div><div class="transcript-line">Well, I just feel like uh there&#39;s there&#39;s a part of a part of everybody that you you never would uh open Pandora&#39;s box. So to speak, I guess, there&#39;s a part of you you never think that you could you could pull the trigger and and kill someone. I mean, when you have to do a s when you have to do something like that, you you lose a part of yourself You have to just let it go and leave it and move on. It takes it takes a l it takes away part of your soul in my eyes.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">24:21</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">24:22</div><div class="transcript-line">I don&#39;t know how to explain it any better, I&#39;m sorry.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">24:24</div><div class="transcript-line">That does that does clarify it a little better for me. Okay. Um If you knew then what you know now, having gone through the entire experience Would you still have gone into the army and as I understood it from the DVD, being a lionist was voluntary?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">24:46</div><div class="transcript-line">Correct.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">24:47</div><div class="transcript-line">And or would you still have volunteered for I wouldn&#39;t I would not change a thing.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">24:53</div><div class="transcript-line">I mean it sucks what happened, but it&#39;s made me a stronger and better person and I thank God every day for it.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">24:59</div><div class="transcript-line">Wow Well.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">25:00</div><div class="transcript-line">Yeah. I mean, everybody wishes things like that wouldn&#39;t happen. But they do.</div><div class="timestamp">25:05</div><div class="transcript-line">So you accept it and you move on. And it&#39;s taught me so much. I know there&#39;s not anything left in life that I can&#39;t accomplish.</div><div class="timestamp">25:11</div><div class="transcript-line">If you can make it through something like that, then You know, you get your head on straight.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">25:15</div><div class="transcript-line">Makes a lot of sense, yeah.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">25:16</div><div class="transcript-line">Yeah.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">25:18</div><div class="transcript-line">Um is there anything that you wanted to address, you know, regarding the film itself um, you know, maybe something that because of time or whatever, um, didn&#39;t make it into the film that you wanted to, you know, add for the record here or Anything that you wanted to address regarding the film at all?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">25:39</div><div class="transcript-line">No, I think they did a good job. We spent way, way too long filming. No, many, many hours. I I think it&#39;s important that uh the women get the recognition they deserve. That&#39;s another thing we talked about in DC also is starting a maybe lioness service ribbon which is something that does not exist. I mean they&#39;re still on even claiming us really, but um but a service ribbon for females in combatant service</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">26:08</div><div class="transcript-line">That&#39;s great. So who brought that up? Was it was it you? Was it a lioness from the government?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">26:12</div><div class="transcript-line">No, it was actually a lady from Florida.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">26:15</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">26:16</div><div class="transcript-line">That is uh prior service. And she has a lot to do with the uh Vietnam veterans of America.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">26:22</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">26:22</div><div class="transcript-line">And uh she actually brought that up. I mean um The the best we get right now is the combat action badge, the cab. It&#39;s kind of like the same thing like a a CIB.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">26:34</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">26:35</div><div class="transcript-line">An infantry badge that the males receive. So now they&#39;re starting to give us cabs. And uh I think, you know, that also comes along with a service ribbon that the men get to wear for the CIB. So I think that was important. Uh the women are out there doing these things and I think they deserve the recognition.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">26:53</div><div class="transcript-line">Absolutely. And and going back to Washington, did they sound like you know, they&#39;re gonna be more proactive absolutely good.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">27:01</div><div class="transcript-line">Absolutely. I think things are gonna move forward pretty fast.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">27:03</div><div class="transcript-line">Did they discuss how how they&#39;re gonna make that happen at all?</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">27:07</div><div class="transcript-line">No, not necess not necessarily, but there&#39;s a lot of chains they&#39;re gonna work it through</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">27:11</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">27:11</div><div class="transcript-line">We talk to the people the exact people you would need to talk to about that.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">27:17</div><div class="transcript-line">Exactly. Good. Yes.</div><div class="timestamp">27:18</div><div class="transcript-line">Good. Okay. Um You know, is there anything that I that I didn&#39;t ask that I should have?</div><div class="timestamp">27:27</div><div class="transcript-line">You covered it. Have I? Okay.</div><div class="timestamp">27:28</div><div class="transcript-line">So there&#39;s nothing that you want to add or anything.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">27:30</div><div class="transcript-line">No, I&#39;m good.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">27:31</div><div class="transcript-line">Okay. All right. Well I think that that covers basically everything that I was going to talk to you about. So thank you very much, Shannon. I appreciate your time.</div><div class="speaker">Shannon Morgan</div><div class="timestamp">27:41</div><div class="transcript-line">Absolutely.</div><div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Gutierrez)</div><div class="timestamp">27:42</div><div class="transcript-line">This concludes our interview.</div>
